<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Goa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Goa is a region on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-de-albuquerque">Afonso de Albuquerque</a> in 1510, it became the capital of the Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estado-da-india">Estado da Índia</a> and the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> in Asia, remaining Portuguese until 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goa.jpg" alt="Goa" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sam 8393 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BeachFun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
